From d1312675c9f810534dcbf72170f3dbddb5f265f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 07:50:53 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: audioreach: send static calibration for every
 module

Commit c7ed4c2debfd ("ASoC: qcom: audioreach: add support for static
calibration") lets a topology carry a blob of calibration data for a
module, a list of parameter records in the APM_CMD_SET_CFG payload
format, and names echo and noise cancellation and speaker protection as
its users. Only MODULE_ID_SMECNS_V2 sends it, though: the blob of any
other module is parsed, kept and never sent, so a topology cannot tune
an equaliser, a limiter or speaker protection that way.

Send the blob for every module that has one, before the module's media
format and the parameters the driver sets itself, so that those keep
precedence over static data. SMECNS_V2 behaves as before, and topologies
without calibration data are unaffected.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
index 0350afb5995a..5cf0775e0b74 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.c
@@ -1447,6 +1447,16 @@ int audioreach_set_media_format(struct q6apm_graph *graph,
 {
 	int rc;
 
+	/*
+	 * Static calibration from the topology first, so that the media
+	 * format and the parameters set below take precedence.
+	 */
+	if (module->data) {
+		rc = audioreach_set_module_config(graph, module, cfg);
+		if (rc)
+			return rc;
+	}
+
 	switch (module->module_id) {
 	case MODULE_ID_DATA_LOGGING:
 		rc = audioreach_module_enable(graph, module, true);
@@ -1463,9 +1473,6 @@ int audioreach_set_media_format(struct q6apm_graph *graph,
 	case MODULE_ID_DISPLAY_PORT_SINK:
 		rc = audioreach_display_port_set_media_format(graph, module, cfg);
 		break;
-	case  MODULE_ID_SMECNS_V2:
-		rc = audioreach_set_module_config(graph, module, cfg);
-		break;
 	case MODULE_ID_I2S_SOURCE:
 	case MODULE_ID_I2S_SINK:
 		rc = audioreach_i2s_set_media_format(graph, module, cfg);
